id: pm-evidence-custom-provider-canonical
title: Canonicalize repeated-dot custom provider source identities
description: "Regression in PR #42: repeated leading dot operands diverge from stored custom descriptors and affected silently skips changed evidence."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,"gh:unbraind/pm-evidence#43",paths
created_at: "2026-11-06T17:51:06.902Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T15:33:18.570Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T17:51:46.198Z",codex-sol,"Read issue #43 in full via REST and inspected origin/main 049dc82. The custom branch of sourceIdentity strips one leading dot slash per call, unlike the idempotent built-in branch. Plan: canonicalize only leading dot prefixes for custom providers, preserve opaque suffixes and legacy persisted records, and verify raw operands, descriptor comparisons and adapter/cache reads through real gitless SDK trackers and the built package."
  "2026-11-06T17:52:23.282Z",codex-sol,"Failing-first proof on unchanged main 049dc82: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/custom-source-paths.test.ts reports 0 pass, 3 fail. Exact issue reproduction returns no affected row; legacy descriptor filtering also skips changed citations. The fix stays in sourceIdentity: remove all leading dot-slash prefixes in one pass, using a dot for a dot-only root, while preserving the opaque suffix. No stored citation rewrite and no dependency changes."
  "2026-11-06T17:55:45.577Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/custom-source-paths-revert.acceptance.ts passed. In a disposable source copy, reverting only the custom sourceIdentity return to PR #42 and rebuilding dist made all 3 regressions fail; restoring the fix and rebuilding made all 3 pass. Linked tests also passed via pm test --run --progress (3/3). Initial duplication gate found repeated fixture setup; extracted one shared custom-tracker fixture and reran the unchanged gate at 0% duplication. Local lint and typecheck passed; full npm and Bun release gates remain CI-owned per task instructions."
  "2026-11-06T17:56:34.702Z",codex-sol,"Final implementation checks: targeted custom and canonical source-path suites passed 18/18; after fixture deduplication, the rebuilt disposable behavioral proof again produced 3 failures on the #42 branch and 3 passes after restoration. Lint, typecheck, docstrings and duplication (0%) passed. The distribution oracle checks committed HEAD too, so it will be rerun after committing the rebuilt artifacts. Full npm/Bun gates run in CI. Implementation is ready for the required queued CodeRabbit review and final-head CI; item remains in progress for orchestrator verification and closure."
  "2026-11-06T17:57:06.160Z",codex-sol,Local pm health additionally reports only extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew between the pinned 2026.11.4 host and ignored managed pm-github metadata at 2026.11.5. The existing pm-evidence-local-extension-skew item already tracks this checkout-only condition; no SDK pin bump or managed-extension change is included. Fresh CI will establish repository tracker health.
  "2026-11-07T00:15:23.338Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched all review threads and comments; one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVUfUaM60sgBw contains two valid findings (legacy retry identity and leading dot/slash identity closure). Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Remote PR head is current with main. Reusing only relevant saved-WIP test fixtures; implementing fixes and disposable behavioral revert proofs, then targeted and full npm/Bun gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-07T00:18:43.359Z",codex-agent,"Failing-first proof against the remote PR implementation: six focused tests ran, three existing regressions passed and all three new regressions failed with assertion errors (legacy cite ID, legacy re-anchor replacement ID, leading-slash normalization). Self-review found re-anchor uses the same incompatible identity check, and custom drive-prefixed suffixes also failed the repeated boundary. The fix shares canonical producer-ID matching between cite/re-anchor, retains a safe relative prefix for opaque slash/drive suffixes, and validates changed operands across the supported provider domains before provider-specific filtering."
  "2026-11-07T00:24:06.461Z",codex-agent,"Focused source/evidence/path suites passed 30/30 after retaining the built-in refusal boundary. Additional self-review found alias-first matching could override an already present exact canonical citation and change recorded re-anchor links; exact ID lookup now precedes compatibility lookup, with a dedicated regression and independent helper-only negative control. Installed a disposable Bun 1.4.4 test runtime because the host default Bun predates the documented Git-consumer minimum. Strict local pm health retains the pre-existing ignored managed-extension skew (pinned host 2026.11.4 versus managed pm-github 2026.11.6); history integrity and drift checks pass. Fresh tracked-only validation will verify repository health independently."
  "2026-11-07T00:30:13.775Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof passed via pm test (3/3 linked commands): disposable copies rebuild dist after every function change. Reverting sourceIdentity to PR #42 fails 3 regressions and restoration passes all 3. Independently reverting cite, review, sourceIdentity and affected to the pre-review PR code fails one behavioral regression each; restoring each function passes it. A helper-only alias-first negative control fails the exact-ID-precedence regression and restoration passes it. Every negative control reaches AssertionError rather than a build/setup failure. Refactored shared legacy fixture setup to preserve the unchanged 0% duplication threshold; rerunning final linked tests after that test-only refactor."
  "2026-11-07T01:13:09.056Z",codex-agent,"Final validation at source commit e9516920949c4696dada41ddad7fa0de5184942f: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/custom-source-paths.test.ts test/custom-source-retry.test.ts test/source-paths.test.ts test/evidence.test.ts passed 31/31; pm test --run --progress --timeout 1200 passed all 3 linked commands after fixture refactoring. Both disposable revert harnesses passed, with 3 original regressions failing/restoring and 5 independent one-failure/one-pass controls. npm run release:check passed in 2381.637 seconds: 200/200 tests, 24 intended source files at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines, 4/4 npm/npx and Bun/bunx packed/Git consumer journeys, 2/2 distribution checks (56 committed artifacts and 168 adversarial mutations), identity zero violations, duplication 0%, typecheck/lint/docstrings/changelog/release attestation passed, and production audit zero vulnerabilities. No local timeout occurred. Bun 1.4.4 was used for consumer acceptance through a disposable runtime. A complete second full coverage run would exceed the combined roughly one-hour local gate budget (coverage alone took 2067.319 seconds), so bun run release:check is delegated to CI under the task time limit. Strict tracked-only self-host health passed 10/10 checks with zero warnings under an isolated home; the normal checkout retains only the previously tracked ignored managed-extension version skew. Source-head CI is pending at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/actions/runs/42322269557 and source-head CodeQL passed at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/actions/runs/42322269561. Review threads were fetched again: the same single unresolved thread contains the original two findings, with no newer review or Outside diff range findings. No finding was refused, no thread replied to or resolved, and no merge or release was performed. The saved local WIP branch was deleted after the code push. No new pm CLI or SDK defect was identified."
  "2026-11-07T10:17:48.331Z",codex-agent,"Re-review: PRRT_kwDOVUfUaM60xHMw is valid. General rule: operator-input normalization and refusal policy must depend on explicit configuration, never on stored records or enumeration order, and must finish before source reads. The current fallback accepts custom-only operands up front but lazily re-normalizes them for built-in citations; built-in-only traversal operands can likewise fail only after encountering a custom citation. Plan: compute both domain filters once before tracker enumeration, retain strict configured-custom traversal refusals, and explicitly report operands restricted to one provider domain in the public scope. Audit SDK, CLI, JSON/TOON, packed consumers and no-git tracker behavior; add corpus/order adversarial tests and a function-only revert proof. The prior fixes, commits and saved-WIP cleanup remain complete."
  "2026-11-07T10:26:21.783Z",codex-agent,"Package-wide audit: affected is the only producer that interprets changed-source operands; native runCommand delegates to it, SDK exports share it, and both JSON/TOON render the same Packet. Other sourceIdentity calls normalize one explicitly selected provider or validated persisted descriptors; none has a second lazy changed-operand policy. Replaced both late-domain failures with one preflight filter computed from explicit adapters. Custom-only operands are visibly restricted by scope.customOnlyChanged; built-in-only operands by scope.builtinOnlyChanged. Configured custom adapters still reject traversal, now before tracker enumeration and source reads. Failing-first on unchanged b724679: both source and built adversarial tests failed with the accepted-custom-operand assertion on a mixed corpus. Fixed tests pass 2/2 across all 65 ordered corpora each, preserving native history, released legacy records and native JSON/TOON behavior. Existing 19 custom/canonical path regressions remain passing; no existing expectation was weakened."
  "2026-11-07T10:35:17.162Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof for the new class regression: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/changed-operands-revert.acceptance.ts passed. A disposable source copy replaces only affected with the b724679 function and rebuilds dist; both source/built tests fail with the mixed-provider behavioral assertion. Restoring affected and rebuilding passes both APIs across all 65 ordered corpora, legacy producer data, early invalid-operand refusals, nonexistent-tracker preflight and JSON/TOON restrictions. This was rerun after the final positive/serialization corpus expansion (93.8 seconds). Focused path/verification/CLI tests passed 32/32 via pinned pm; the two new linked commands passed 2/2, with earlier completed linked commands intentionally excluded by --match changed-operands. Typecheck, lint, docstrings (128 declarations) and zero-duplication passed at unchanged thresholds. The same contract has been added to all four packed/Git npm/Bun consumer journeys; targeted consumer validation and refreshed full gates follow."
  "2026-11-07T10:41:02.597Z",codex-agent,"Targeted packed-consumer validation caught an issue in the newly added secondary tracker setup before the contract ran. Its activation now installs the already captured and integrity-verified archive, rather than installing an external dependency directory as another managed extension. A real bare gitless tracker accepted archive activation with zero blocking health failures. The original packed/Git npm/Bun install paths and all existing assertions remain unchanged; diagnostics now include native stdout as well as stderr. No package runtime code changed during this fixture correction."
  "2026-11-07T10:47:13.514Z",codex-agent,"Expanded packed-consumer verification passed 2/2: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern \"^packed \" test/install.acceptance.ts, using Node and Bun 1.4.4 with isolated Git/home configuration. Both real installed consumers execute the exact shared 65-corpus contract, including released legacy data, native CLI JSON/TOON, explicit domain scope and durable-history preservation. The secondary tracker uses the captured verified archive. The ordinary consumer typecheck remains strict; allowImportingTsExtensions permits the added runnable TypeScript contract. All pre-existing install assertions remain present. Full release gates are refreshed next at unchanged thresholds, with the original roughly one-hour local-gate bound retained."
  "2026-11-07T11:39:05.787Z",codex-agent,"Re-review final gates at 4b15a9613a05fe1438ff190ce4c02e3319e7c6b9: npm run release:check passed in 3000.211 seconds (50.0 minutes), with 202/202 tests and all 24 intended source files at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. All four packed/Git npm/npx and Bun/bunx journeys passed the shared 65-corpus contract; the six source/built/installed API variants collectively cover 390 ordered corpus cases. Distribution passed 2/2 (56 committed artifacts, 168 adversarial mutations refused); duplication remained 0%; typecheck, lint, docstrings, identity/privacy, changelog and release attestation passed; production audit found zero vulnerabilities. There were no local timeouts. Bun 1.4.4 consumer acceptance is measured, while a complete second bun run release:check is delegated to CI under the original roughly one-hour combined local gate bound: coverage alone took 2662.682 seconds. Fresh final-head CI remains pending; follow https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/pull/44/checks. The existing ignored local managed-extension version skew remains separately tracked. All findings in this round were valid and fixed; no review-thread reply, resolution, merge or release was performed. Prior completed fixes and saved-WIP cleanup were preserved. No new pm CLI/SDK defect was confirmed; the additional fixture activation uses the supported verified-archive path."
  "2026-11-07T14:40:41.903Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 2: PRRT_kwDOVUfUaM601ueD is a valid regression-coverage request, not a demonstrated runtime defect. General rule: citation identity and compatibility reuse remain scoped to the owning item and provider; exact IDs take priority, then the first qualifying genuine legacy alias in persisted citation order is reused. The branch was behind the release commit; merged origin/main first and regenerated the conflicting changelog without editing any history stream. Plan: adversarial public-API tests across two owners, colliding provider/source/byte descriptors and alias order, with cite/re-anchor/retention, native JSON/TOON, installed npm/Bun consumers and real gitless trackers. Preserve matching behavior and all prior tests. Function-only mutation controls will prove the existing identity guards and tie policy are necessary; a behavior revert cannot fail for a tests-only coverage addition."
  "2026-11-07T15:01:02.472Z",codex-agent,"Whole-class audit: searched citation IDs, descriptor/digest comparisons, owner admission and provenance rebinding throughout src and the complete PR diff. cite and re-anchor share existingCitation; Store state validates the canonical owning item before matching; provider remains in both identity generation and descriptor comparison. Other citationById consumers read the validated owned state. Bundle preview and apply share plan/imported and explicitly rebind target ownership, preserving provider identity. No additional runtime defect was demonstrated. Added real gitless public-API coverage with two owners, three colliding providers, all 24 custom-alias orders plus exact-ID cases, byte/history no-op checks, retention upgrades and authorized import recipients. Native CLI JSON/TOON and every packed/Git npm/Bun consumer execute the same contract. Current nonblocking finding is valid coverage work; matching behavior is preserved."
  "2026-11-07T15:02:13.244Z",codex-agent,"Mutation/revert proof: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/citation-reuse-controls.acceptance.ts passed 1/1 in 218.157 seconds. Disposable source copies mutate only one function at a time and rebuild dist: prepare without owner identity; prepare without provider identity; existingCitation without provider comparison; existingCitation choosing the last alias; Store state without owner admission; imported without target-owner identity; imported without provider identity. All seven controls fail with a behavioral AssertionError. After restoring every function and rebuilding, the source and built contracts pass 2/2 across the full 24-order matrix and native JSON/TOON checks. This round adds tests and policy documentation only; there is no runtime behavior change whose revert should fail. Existing released legacy fixture IDs are preserved. Typecheck, lint, 128 documented declarations and 0% duplication passed at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-07T15:05:01.887Z",codex-agent,"Focused validation through pinned pm passed 12/12: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/citation-reuse.test.ts test/custom-source-retry.test.ts test/changed-operands.test.ts test/bundles.test.ts (156.0 seconds). Prior linked commands were intentionally not rerun. Fresh tracked-only self-host health with isolated home/Git configuration exits zero; one advisory pending-telemetry-queue receipt remains, with no blocking health failure or merge receipt pending. Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so the measured result is recorded here instead of enabling run records in the package tracker. Next: real packed npm/Bun consumers, then the full Bun launcher release gate; a duplicate full npm launcher run is delegated to CI because the last measured full run consumed 50 minutes and the original combined local-gate budget is about one hour."
  "2026-11-07T15:16:50.890Z",codex-agent,"Packed consumers passed 2/2 at 1011b15: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern \"^packed \" test/install.acceptance.ts. npm/npx took 315.8 seconds and Bun/bunx 334.1 seconds; total 650.95 seconds, with the expanded shared contract and exact 56-artifact graph verified for both. No timeouts occurred. This measured 10.8-minute pair changes the local full-gate forecast: four such journeys plus the prior 44.4-minute coverage stage exceed 66 minutes before remaining gates. Under the original roughly-one-hour conditional full-gate rule, both complete release launchers are delegated to final-head CI; the earlier plan to rerun a full Bun launcher locally is superseded by this measurement. Complete the remaining Git npm/Bun acceptance and mandatory focused/static/self-host checks locally instead; preserve every threshold."
  "2026-11-07T15:22:49.556Z",codex-agent,"Git consumer run: npm/npx passed in 269.4 seconds. Bun failed before consumer execution because pinned pm test supplied system Bun 1.3.5 despite the outer prepared PATH; the Git dependency resolver reported no matching commit. The already completed direct packed journey used prepared Bun 1.4.4 and passed. Retry only Git Bun with an explicit supported pm test --env-set PATH override, keeping the successful npm evidence and all test assertions unchanged. This is runner configuration evidence, not a demonstrated package or SDK defect; no timeout occurred."
  "2026-11-07T15:25:38.764Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the previous runner diagnosis: the temporary prepared Bun binary no longer existed; PATH lookup therefore fell through to system Bun 1.3.5. The explicit PATH retry and a direct-run check reproduced the same fallback, so pm test was not the cause. No pm CLI/SDK defect is established. The completed npm packed/Git results stand. Earlier packed Bun passed, but its exact runtime version was not captured reliably and is superseded by a fresh isolated Bun 1.4.4 run. Installed and verified a new disposable binary; the gate wrapper now refuses immediately if that binary is missing or is not 1.4.4. Rerun only both Bun consumer journeys, keeping all assertions and the valid npm evidence."
  "2026-11-07T15:33:10.990Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 results at code head 1011b15c4db04468f357cdf68cff460cf5963e67: all four unique installed consumer journeys pass. Packed npm/npx 315.763 seconds and Git npm/npx 269.397 seconds; verified isolated Bun 1.4.4 passed packed Bun/bunx 202.700 seconds and Git Bun/bunx 184.506 seconds, via node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=bun test/install.acceptance.ts through pinned pm with explicit runtime environment (2/2, 389.366 seconds). Both running Bun consumer executables were independently observed to match the verified binary. Earlier Git Bun attempts on fallback 1.3.5 failed dependency resolution before consumer execution; the 1.4.4 retry supersedes those environment failures. No local timeout occurred. The valid focused command passed 12/12; mutation harness 1/1 with all seven behavioral negative controls and restored APIs 2/2; distribution 2/2 with 56 pristine artifacts and 168 adversarial mutations refused. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 128 documented declarations, zero-vulnerability production audit, package dry run and release attestation all pass at unchanged thresholds. No runtime code change was needed for this valid coverage request; existing matcher guarantees and all previous fixes are preserved. No new pm CLI/SDK defect was confirmed."
  "2026-11-07T15:33:14.349Z",codex-agent,"Full-gate disposition after the verified runtime retry: the four consumer journeys total 16.2 minutes; adding the prior measured 44.4-minute coverage stage forecasts at least 60.6 minutes per launcher before the new regression coverage and remaining checks. Both full npm and Bun launchers together exceed the original approximately-one-hour local full-gate budget, so final-head CI certifies those gates and current coverage: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/pull/44/checks. The historical npm full gate at 4b15a96 passed 202 tests and 100/100/100/100 across all 24 intended sources; it is not represented as current-head coverage. Latest review pagination was complete, with one unresolved valid coverage thread PRRT_kwDOVUfUaM601ueD and no outside-diff findings. Main was merged first; saved-WIP cleanup and prior completed work were preserved. Remaining risk: final-head CI pending; existing ignored local extension-version skew remains separately tracked, and tracked-only health has an advisory pending telemetry receipt with no blocking failure. Release this claim without closing the item. No thread reply/resolution, PR merge or release was performed."
